Phase A: rich-text editor + Supabase image upload for blog admin

WHAT
admin/blog now ships with Quill (CDN, snow theme) replacing the raw
HTML textarea. The toolbar has:
  - Headings (H2, H3) + paragraph
  - Bold / italic / underline
  - Blockquote
  - Ordered + bullet lists
  - Alignment (left / center / right / justify)
  - Link
  - Image (uploads to Supabase Storage, see below)
  - Clean (strip formatting)

A "Raw HTML" toggle is still available for power users — switches between
the visual editor and the existing textarea without losing content.

IMAGE UPLOAD
New `uploadBlogImage(file)` helper on KANAAN_ADMIN posts the file to a
new `blog-images` Supabase Storage bucket (public read, authenticated
write). The Quill image button calls this helper, then inserts the
public URL into the editor — no base64 embedding.

The Hero image field also gets an "⬆ Upload" button and a live preview
thumbnail so the admin can replace the hero with a single file pick.

DEPLOY STEP
Run the new migration in the Supabase SQL editor to create the bucket
and RLS policies:
  supabase/migrations/20260519100000_blog_images_bucket.sql

The 5 MB / image-types limits are enforced both client-side (in
uploadBlogImage) and server-side (bucket config).

CSS
assets/css/blog.css now styles Quill's alignment classes
(.ql-align-center / -right / -justify) and inline images so admin-typed
formatting renders correctly on /blog and /blog/<slug>.

NOTE ON SCOPE
This is Phase A of the user's bigger "everything editable" ask. The
storage bucket + upload helper are reusable — subsequent phases (offers,
branches, banners, testimonials, site config, service pages, etc.) can
reuse the same upload mechanism for their own images without a new
bucket per area.

